[{:db/id 17592186092066 :question/worked-solution "The counterclockwise rotation $\\mathbf{R}_{\\pi}$ by an angle of $\\pi$ radians is given by the matrix\n\n![](images/a5/a5b5bd722e0f84e175af70516d25edbcdbe55b48cbbb0ee7821d03272afac1ff.svg)\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of $\\mathbf{R}_{\\pi},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S$ as columns:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $\\mathbf{R}_{\\pi}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -5 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $S'$ are $(-2,1), (3,-5), (-4,3).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092114 :question/problem "![](images/a4/a43a1658a16151c0306702959c50e8d0288077983ad50a084b39703e206469c0.png)\n\nConsider the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ shown above. Find the vector $A\\mathbf{v}$ given that \n![](images/ac/ac8c8fcdf75b72b65ceadb1d500625d4414264973876c10bf47c47a8e418ffd7.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092223 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-08bf8696-2d24-58a9-b5b4-856286859054"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092065 :question/worked-solution "The clockwise rotation $\\mathbf{R}_{-90^\\circ}$ by an angle of $90^\\circ$ is the same as counterclockwise rotation by an angle of $270^\\circ.$ It's given by the matrix\n\n![](images/7f/7f8b60362b08e038452b3454b1719c6f51df7d0129cc7d957e328a92b4f7e7c3.svg)\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of $\\mathbf{R}_{-90^\\circ},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S$ as columns:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $\\mathbf{R}_{-90^\\circ}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $S'$ are $(-1,5), (4,-1), (-5,-3).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-08bf8696-2d24-58a9-b5b4-856286859054" :question/id #uuid "08bf8696-2d24-58a9-b5b4-856286859054" :question/math-academy-id "q-160646" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at  $(-1,3),(-2,2),(1,-4).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the **clockwise** rotation ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${90}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n\n- $(3,1)$\n- $(2,-2)$\n- $(-4,-1)$" :question/worked-solution "The clockwise rotation ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${90}^{∘}$ is the same as counterclockwise rotation by an angle of ${270}^{∘}.$ It's given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(3,1),(2,2),(-4,-1).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7fc3ccce-1ebd-5f22-9b8f-6e3842468c4d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7fc3ccce-1ebd-5f22-9b8f-6e3842468c4d" :answer-field/id #uuid "7fc3ccce-1ebd-5f22-9b8f-6e3842468c4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-99a9553b-c748-5118-a8d9-ca0c58ba4325" :answer-field/choices ["answer-99a9553b-c748-5118-a8d9-ca0c58ba4325" "answer-7699eaf3-de8c-5053-898a-a4c8beee968f" "answer-10cf90fb-e29e-510d-8cf4-93075f7dd6be" "answer-eadf43e5-1274-5818-a95a-76c46e2e08da" "answer-e9ef7977-1930-5dd3-9b84-4d0b1b641d43"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99a9553b-c748-5118-a8d9-ca0c58ba4325" :answer/id #uuid "99a9553b-c748-5118-a8d9-ca0c58ba4325" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7699eaf3-de8c-5053-898a-a4c8beee968f" :answer/id #uuid "7699eaf3-de8c-5053-898a-a4c8beee968f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-10cf90fb-e29e-510d-8cf4-93075f7dd6be" :answer/id #uuid "10cf90fb-e29e-510d-8cf4-93075f7dd6be" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eadf43e5-1274-5818-a95a-76c46e2e08da" :answer/id #uuid "eadf43e5-1274-5818-a95a-76c46e2e08da" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9ef7977-1930-5dd3-9b84-4d0b1b641d43" :answer/id #uuid "e9ef7977-1930-5dd3-9b84-4d0b1b641d43" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092430 :activity/expected-seconds 660.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
